# Custom traits

## Write C# only as a last resort

First search `engine/OpenRA.Mods.Common/Traits/` for an existing trait. The engine
covers far more than is obvious, and stock traits require no rebuild. Only add C# when
nothing stock can do the job.

## Rebuild after every change

```bash
make RUNTIME=net6
```

Output goes to `engine/bin/OpenRA.Mods.Example.dll`, which `mods/fracturedsteel/mod.yaml`
loads via `Assemblies:`. YAML-only changes do **not** need a rebuild; C# changes always
do. Note this restores NuGet packages and needs unrestricted network access.

## Trait shape

Every trait is a pair: an `Info` class carrying the YAML fields, and the trait itself.

```csharp
public class MyTraitInfo : TraitInfo
{
    [FieldLoader.Require]
    [Desc("Shown in the trait documentation.")]
    public readonly string Image = null;

    public override object Create(ActorInitializer init) { return new MyTrait(init.Self, this); }
}

public class MyTrait : IRender, ITick { /* ... */ }
```

- Public `readonly` fields on the `Info` class map 1:1 to YAML keys.
- Always add `[Desc(...)]`; it is the generated documentation.
- Derive from `ConditionalTraitInfo` to get free `RequiresCondition` support.

## Rendering layers

`IRender` draws in the **world** layer, so a negative `ZOffset` puts a sprite beneath the
actor. `WithDecoration` and other decorations always draw in the top annotation layer and
cannot be placed under a unit — this is why `WithSelectionRing` exists.

